+## What it does
+
+- **Teammates** have a brain, a persona and a toolbox, message each other, and pass people's role checks.
+- **Toolboxes** grant any MCP server or OpenAPI service as `read`, `ask` or `off`; policies only narrow them.
+- **Peter** plans each goal with a model (and may ask questions first) or by role, and re-plans what fails.
+- **Reviews** go hunk by hunk with checks; on GitHub or GitLab an approval opens the pull or merge request,
+  and merging stays with you.
+- **One event stream** per company feeds activity, the office view and costs, with token budgets per company,
+  department, project and teammate.
+- **Roles** (owner, admin, reviewer, viewer) and sign-in through OpenID Connect.
+
+## How it fits together
+
+```text
+browser ──▶ web ──/api──▶ board ──────▶ connections (MCP, OpenAPI), git hosts, webhooks
+                          ▲   │
+            claim runs,   │   │ state, events
+            events, files │   ▼
+                       workers ──────▶ Postgres (every row, the events, the run queue)
+                          │
+                          ▼
+                      model API
+```
+
+- **board** (`apps/board`): owns all state and events, runs Peter, reviews and approvals, alone calls
+  connections.
+- **web** (`apps/web`): the React app behind nginx, which proxies `/api` to the board.
+- **workers** (`apps/worker`): run a teammate's engine headless; on a cluster they reach nothing private.
+- **Postgres**: rows, events, sessions and the queue; an S3 bucket is optional, for artifacts over 512 KB.
+
+The [operator guide](docs/operator.md) has each part in full.
+
+## Engines
+
+Each teammate runs on an engine, and only real engines need anything:
+
+| Engine          | What the worker needs                                                                                         |
+| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| Stub (no model) | Nothing. It writes the task's declared outputs and a handover; no model, no tokens, no cost.                  |
+| Claude Code     | The `claude` CLI, signed in (`claude auth login`), or `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` or `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` for it |
+| Codex           | The `codex` CLI, signed in (`codex login`), or `OPENAI_API_KEY` for it                                        |
+
+Peter needs nothing either: without a model he plans by role; with `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` on the board, or a
+signed-in `claude` or `codex` CLI where it runs, he may use one (Settings > Peter). The worker image built from `apps/worker/Dockerfile` carries Codex; Claude Code's licence keeps it out
+of public images, so add it in your own ([Engines on the worker](docs/install.md#engines-on-the-worker)).
+
